# Managed by Ansible (roles/firewall) - DOCKER-USER IPv6 lockdown.
#
# ASCII ONLY: written into /etc/ufw/after6.rules, which ufw re-serializes with
# an ascii-only encoder on every `ufw default ...` call. A non-ASCII byte here
# crashes that call with UnicodeEncodeError on the second apply. Keep every
# character within 0x00-0x7F.
#
# What: Blocks off-host IPv6 traffic to Docker-published ports.
# Why:  Every scope:docker source in this lab's firewall_rules_* is an IPv4
#       CIDR (monitoring_host, etc. - see design spec "Known Docker-published
#       ports"), so there is nothing to allow here, only to deny: any IPv6
#       traffic arriving via {{ ansible_default_ipv4.interface }} (the interface
#       name is protocol-agnostic - same NIC, no separate ansible_default_ipv6
#       fact needed) at DOCKER-USER is off-host and unexpected.
# Resolves: an IPv6-only path around the IPv4-only allowlist above.
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
-A DOCKER-USER -i {{ ansible_default_ipv4.interface }} -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -j RETURN
